        {
          "@type": "ListItem",
          position: 3,
          name: "Kirkland Protein Powder Review",
          item: `${SITE_URL}/kirkland-protein-powder-review/`,
        },
      ],
    },
    {
      "@type": "FAQPage",
      mainEntity: [
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Who makes Kirkland protein powder?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Costco does not name the manufacturer on the bag or its product pages, and we could not find a reliable public source that does. Websites naming a specific maker did not cite evidence. Like most store brands, Kirkland whey is made by a contract supplier to Costco's specifications, so you rely on Costco's supplier standards and satisfaction guarantee rather than a brand's public testing record."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Is Kirkland protein powder good?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "For most Costco members, yes. Per the label it gives about 25 g of protein, 130 calories and 1 g of sugar per scoop from an isolate-led whey blend, close to Optimum Nutrition Gold Standard, at roughly $0.70 per 25 g at warehouse prices. It is a poor fit for drug-tested athletes and anyone avoiding sucralose."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How much protein is in Kirkland whey protein?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "The Creamy Chocolate label lists 25 g of protein in a 35 g scoop, with 130 calories, 4 g of carbohydrate, 1 g of fiber, 1 g of sugar and 2 g of fat, at the time of writing. The 5.4 lb bag holds about 70 servings, or roughly 1,750 g of protein in total. The front of the bag claims 5.6 g of BCAAs per scoop."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Can you buy Kirkland protein powder on Amazon?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Not from Costco. Our Amazon search for Kirkland Signature whey returned only other brands. Any Kirkland bags on marketplace sites come from third-party resellers, typically at a markup and without Costco's guarantee. The closest Amazon alternative is Optimum Nutrition Gold Standard 5 lb, and Nutricost's 5 lb concentrate was the cheapest per gram when we checked."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Is Kirkland protein powder third-party tested?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "We could not find Kirkland Signature whey in the NSF Certified for Sport, Informed Sport or Informed Choice databases at the time of writing, and the bag shows no certification logo. Costco runs internal quality checks, but they are not published. Drug-tested athletes should choose a certified powder, such as Ascent, and confirm the exact flavor in the certifier's database."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What sweetener is in Kirkland protein powder?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Kirkland whey is sweetened with sucralose and acesulfame potassium, per the ingredient lists on the US chocolate and Canadian vanilla bags. Both are common in budget whey, including Aldi's Elevation and Dymatize Elite. If you want to avoid artificial sweeteners, choose an unflavored whey such as Nutricost's or a stevia-sweetened brand such as Ascent."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Does Costco sell a Kirkland plant protein powder?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Not that we could find. In the US, the Kirkland protein powder range is one whey, in Creamy Chocolate, and Costco Canada adds a vanilla whey. Costco's plant protein shelf is stocked by other brands, mainly Orgain in the US. Kirkland also sells protein bars, and a Kirkland protein shake has launched in Costco Canada."
          }
        }
      ],
