              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Buying Kirkland from a reseller</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Kirkland Signature whey is not sold by Costco on Amazon or any other marketplace. Reseller listings usually carry a markup that erases the saving, and you cannot know how the bag was stored or how old it is. Without a membership, a real Amazon alternative is the better buy.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Assuming isolate-led means lactose-free</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Kirkland's blend lists whey isolate first, but it also contains whey concentrate, which keeps more lactose. Most people with mild sensitivity cope fine, but if regular whey bloats you, start with half a scoop or choose a pure isolate rather than committing to a 5.4 lb bag.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Treating a house brand as certified</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Costco's quality control is internal, and we could not find Kirkland whey in any sport certification database. If you are drug tested, buy a product listed by NSF Certified for Sport or Informed Sport, search the exact product and flavor in the certifier's database, and keep your batch number.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Comparing price per bag, not per 25 g</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                A $50 bag and a $106 tub are not comparable until you divide by servings and protein per serving. Work out cost per 25 g of protein, and include delivery fees, because a same-day Costco delivery price can push Kirkland much closer to name-brand territory.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Committing to 70 servings blind</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Kirkland comes in one US flavor and one big size, so a bag you dislike is two months of shakes. Mix the first scoops with milk, try it in coffee or oatmeal, and remember Costco's satisfaction guarantee if the bag turns out to be genuinely undrinkable for you.
              </p>
            </div>
